<title>USA: Top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>Top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-03-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are ticket sales for the top movies at the box office over the weekend, according to estimates by Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    1 (*) Return of the Jedi ............... $16.3 million</p>
<p>    2 (2) Jungle 2 Jungle .................. $11.3 million</p>
<p>    3 (1) Private Parts ....................  $9.0 million</p>
<p>    4=(3) The Empire Strikes Back ..........  $5.5 million</p>
<p>    4=(4) Donnie Brasco ....................  $5.5 million</p>
<p>    6 (*) Love Jones .......................  $4.0 million</p>
<p>    7(16) Sling Blade ......................  $3.0 million</p>
<p>    8 (7) Absolute Power ...................  $2.5 million</p>
<p>    9 (6) Star Wars ........................  $2.3 million</p>
<p>    10(5) Booty Call .......................  $2.2 million</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures in parentheses are last week's rank.</p>
<p>&quot;Return of the Jedi,&quot; &quot;The Empire Strikes Back&quot; and &quot;Star Wars&quot; released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp. .</p>
<p>&quot;Jungle 2 Jungle&quot; released by Walt Disney Co. and &quot;Sling Blade&quot; is released by Disney's Miramax Films.</p>
<p>&quot;Private Parts&quot; released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;Donnie Brasco,&quot; &quot;Absolute Power&quot; and &quot;Booty Call&quot; are released by Sony Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Love Jones&quot; is from New Line Cinema, a unit of Time Warner Inc.</p>
